  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 206 PM CST Sat Nov 7 2026\n\nWarmer temperatures only look to last through Tuesday as ensemble \nguidance signals a longwave trough expanding over the eastern US \nlater this week. Surface low-pressure associated with this trough \nwill shift winds to become northerly, and with that, ample cold-air \nadvection. Nocturnal radiative cooling and relatively clear skies \ncould allow overnight low temperatures for the second half of the \nweek to fall below freezing. Much of the area is expected to remain \ndry through the week, but shortwaves associated with the changing \nweather pattern may induce periods of additional cloud cover and \nlow chances for precipitation (10-20%).",
